issue_2_text:
Observations page Promise.all fails entirely if a single experiment fetch errors
## Bug Description

In observations/page.js, the `Promise.all()` (line 43) wraps ALL observation mapping operations. If ANY single experiment fails to fetch (deleted experiment, network error, server 500), the entire `Promise.all` rejects and the user sees NO observations at all.

## Affected Code
```javascript
// observations/page.js, line 43
const tableViews = await Promise.all(data.map(async (obs) => {
    // ...
    const expData = await fetchExperimentData(labId, eId);
    // If this throws for one obs, the whole page breaks
    // ...
}));
```

## Impact
- One orphaned or deleted experiment causes all other valid observations to disappear
- Error is silently swallowed (only logged to console)
- User cannot access ANY of their saved observations

## Fix
Use `Promise.allSettled()` instead of `Promise.all()` to process failures individually:
```javascript
const results = await Promise.allSettled(data.map(async (obs) => {
    // ...
}));
const tableViews = results
    .filter(r => r.status === 'fulfilled' && r.value)
    .map(r => r.value);
```

Crash on null experiment_id in starred and history pages
## Bug Description

Both starred/page.js and history/page.js call `.includes('/')` on `item.experiment_id` without null checking.

## Affected Code
```javascript
// starred/page.js, lines 43-45
if (item.experiment_id.includes('/')) {
    [labId, expId] = item.experiment_id.split('/');
}
```
```javascript
// history/page.js, lines 38-40  
if (item.experiment_id.includes('/')) {
    [labId, expId] = item.experiment_id.split('/');
}
```

## Impact
- If a database record has `experiment_id = null` or `undefined`, calling `.includes('/')` will throw `TypeError: Cannot read properties of null/undefined`
- This crashes the entire page, not just the affected item
- The `.filter(Boolean)` at the end only filters items that are null/undefined AFTER processing, but the crash happens BEFORE that

## Fix
```javascript
const expId_raw = item.experiment_id;
if (!expId_raw) return null;
if (String(expId_raw).includes('/')) {
    [labId, expId] = String(expId_raw).split('/');
}
```

Memory leak: setTimeout not cleared on component unmount in observations/starred/history pages
## Bug Description

The `fetchObservations()`, `fetchStarred()`, and `fetchHistory()` functions all create safety timeouts (lines 32-35, etc.) but these are local variables that are NOT cleared when the component unmounts.

## Affected Code
```javascript
// observations/page.js, line 32
const fetchObservations = async () => {
    const timeout = setTimeout(() => {
        setLoading(false);
        console.warn('Fetch timed out for observations');
    }, 8000);
    // ... timeout is NOT cleared in finally block OR on unmount
```

## Impact
- If a user navigates away before the fetch completes, the timeout callback fires on an unmounted component
- React will log a warning about state update on unmounted component
- In strict mode (dev), this happens twice, potentially corrupting state in parent components
- The effect cleanup only removes the `workspace-updated` event listener, not the pending timeout

## Fix
```javascript
const fetchRef = useRef(null);

useEffect(() => {
    fetchObservations();
    return () => {
        if (fetchRef.current) clearTimeout(fetchRef.current);
    };
}, [user, authLoading]);
```

Observations page Promise.all fails entirely if a single experiment fetch errors
## Bug Description

In observations/page.js, the `Promise.all()` (line 43) wraps ALL observation mapping operations. If ANY single experiment fails to fetch (deleted experiment, network error, server 500), the entire `Promise.all` rejects and the user sees NO observations at all.

## Affected Code
```javascript
// observations/page.js, line 43
const tableViews = await Promise.all(data.map(async (obs) => {
    // ...
    const expData = await fetchExperimentData(labId, eId);
    // If this throws for one obs, the whole page breaks
    // ...
}));
```

## Impact
- One orphaned or deleted experiment causes all other valid observations to disappear
- Error is silently swallowed (only logged to console)
- User cannot access ANY of their saved observations

## Fix
Use `Promise.allSettled()` instead of `Promise.all()` to process failures individually:
```javascript
const results = await Promise.allSettled(data.map(async (obs) => {
    // ...
}));
const tableViews = results
    .filter(r => r.status === 'fulfilled' && r.value)
    .map(r => r.value);
```

Crash on null experiment_id in starred and history pages
