issue_2_text:
Marketplace listing submission is a client-side stub — images collected but never uploaded
## Description

The `AddListingScreen` in `frontend/lib/screens/marketplace/add_listing_screen.dart` collects all listing data (title, price, description, images, category, condition) but the `_submitListing` method performs zero actual submission. It simulates a 2-second delay and navigates back, discarding all user input.

## Affected Files
- `frontend/lib/screens/marketplace/add_listing_screen.dart` lines 46-66
- `frontend/lib/services/marketplace/marketplace_service.dart` — does not exist (commented out import at line 7)

## Current Code (line 46-66):
```dart
Future<void> _submitListing() async {
  if (!_formKey.currentState!.validate()) return;
  if (_images.isEmpty) {
    ScaffoldMessenger.of(context).showSnackBar(
        const SnackBar(content: Text("Please add at least one image")));
    return;
  }

  setState(() => _isUploading = true);

  // Call service to upload listing with images
  // await ref.read(marketplaceServiceProvider).createListing(...);

  // Simulate delay
  await Future.delayed(const Duration(seconds: 2));

  if (mounted) {
    setState(() => _isUploading = false);
    Navigator.pop(context);
  }
}
```

## Evidence the backend works
The backend `listingResource.js` (lines 13-39) has a fully functional POST endpoint that accepts title, description, price, category, condition, and image uploads via Cloudinary. The issue is entirely on the frontend.

## Impact
Users see a working form, click "Post Listing", see a loading spinner, and are redirected — but nothing is actually created. The marketplace listing creation feature is completely broken for end users.

## Recommended Fix
1. Create the missing `marketplace_service.dart` that calls the backend POST endpoint
2. Wire it into `_submitListing`
3. Upload the selected images and pass all collected form data to the backend

