issue_2_text:
Runtime crash: Wishlist endpoint hits MissingSchemaError for unregistered 'Student' model
## Bug Description
The wishlist toggle endpoint crashes with `MissingSchemaError` on every request because it references the `Student` model which was never registered or imported.

## Affected File
`backend/resources/marketplace/listingResource.js:154`

## Problem
During the migration to a unified `User` model, the wishlist route still tries to use `mongoose.model("Student")`. Since `Student` was never imported or registered in this file, any `PUT /api/v1/listings/:id/wishlist` request immediately crashes with:
```
MissingSchemaError: Schema hasn't been registered for model "Student". Use mongoose.model(name, schema)
```

## Steps to Reproduce
1. Login to the app (any valid user)
2. Navigate to marketplace
3. Click wishlist/heart icon on any listing
4. Observe 500 Internal Server Error

## Current Code
```javascript
// listingResource.js:154
const Student = mongoose.model("Student");
const student = await Student.findById(userId);

if (!student) return res.status(404).json({ status: false, message: "User not found" });

const index = student.wishlist.indexOf(listingId);
```

## Proposed Fix
The `isAuthenticated` middleware already populates `req.user` as a full Mongoose document on the `User` model. Use it directly instead of querying a non-existent model:

```javascript
const user = req.user; // Already a Mongoose doc from isAuthenticated

if (!user.wishlist) user.wishlist = [];

const index = user.wishlist.indexOf(listingId);
if (index === -1) {
    user.wishlist.push(listingId);
} else {
    user.wishlist.splice(index, 1);
}

await user.save({ validateBeforeSave: false });
```

Then add a `wishlist: [{ type: mongoose.Schema.Types.ObjectId, ref: 'Listing' }]` field to the `User` schema in `models/user.js`.

## Priority
HIGH — This is a user-facing feature that completely fails on every invocation.

