issue_2_text:
Marketplace listing submission is a client-side stub — images collected but never uploaded
## Description

The `AddListingScreen` in `frontend/lib/screens/marketplace/add_listing_screen.dart` collects all listing data (title, price, description, images, category, condition) but the `_submitListing` method performs zero actual submission. It simulates a 2-second delay and navigates back, discarding all user input.

## Affected Files
- `frontend/lib/screens/marketplace/add_listing_screen.dart` lines 46-66
- `frontend/lib/services/marketplace/marketplace_service.dart` — does not exist (commented out import at line 7)

## Current Code (line 46-66):
```dart
Future<void> _submitListing() async {
  if (!_formKey.currentState!.validate()) return;
  if (_images.isEmpty) {
    ScaffoldMessenger.of(context).showSnackBar(
        const SnackBar(content: Text("Please add at least one image")));
    return;
  }

  setState(() => _isUploading = true);

  // Call service to upload listing with images
  // await ref.read(marketplaceServiceProvider).createListing(...);

  // Simulate delay
  await Future.delayed(const Duration(seconds: 2));

  if (mounted) {
    setState(() => _isUploading = false);
    Navigator.pop(context);
  }
}
```

## Evidence the backend works
The backend `listingResource.js` (lines 13-39) has a fully functional POST endpoint that accepts title, description, price, category, condition, and image uploads via Cloudinary. The issue is entirely on the frontend.

## Impact
Users see a working form, click "Post Listing", see a loading spinner, and are redirected — but nothing is actually created. The marketplace listing creation feature is completely broken for end users.

## Recommended Fix
1. Create the missing `marketplace_service.dart` that calls the backend POST endpoint
2. Wire it into `_submitListing`
3. Upload the selected images and pass all collected form data to the backend

issue_1_text:
Security: Message API has no authentication — unauthenticated sender impersonation possible
## Security Vulnerability
The messages API endpoint has no authentication middleware, allowing any user to impersonate any other user and view all messages.

## Affected File
`backend/resources/chatroom/messageListResource.js:14, 31-61`

## Problem

### 1. Unauthenticated message reading
```javascript
// Line 14 — No auth middleware
messageListRouter.get("/", async (req, res) => {
    const allMessages = await Message.find({}).lean();
    // ...
});
```
Anyone can fetch ALL messages in the system without being logged in.

### 2. Sender impersonation via unauthenticated POST
```javascript
// Lines 31-61 — No auth middleware, sender from request body
messageListRouter.post("/", [body("sender").notEmpty()...], async (req, res) => {
    const { sender, content, timestamp } = req.body;
    const newMessage = await Message.create({ sender, content, ... });
    ...
});
```
No authentication required. The `sender` is read directly from the request body, so anyone can forge messages appearing to be from any user.

### 3. Arbitrary deletion
```javascript
messageListRouter.delete("/:id", ...);
```
No auth check — anyone can delete any message by ID.

## Proposed Fix
```javascript
// Add auth middleware to ALL routes
messageListRouter.use(isAuthenticated);

// GET: Filter by authenticated user
messageListRouter.get("/", async (req, res) => {
    const messages = await Message.find({ 
        $or: [{ sender: req.user._id }, { recipient: req.user._id }]
    });
    ...
});

// POST: Derive sender from authenticated user
messageListRouter.post("/", async (req, res) => {
    const { content, recipient, timestamp } = req.body;
    const newMessage = await Message.create({
        sender: req.user._id,  // NOT from request body
        recipient,
        content,
        timestamp: timestamp || new Date(),
    });
    ...
});

// DELETE: Only sender or admin can delete
messageListRouter.delete("/:id", async (req, res) => {
    const message = await Message.findById(req.params.id);
    if (!message || (message.sender.toString() !== req.user._id.toString() 
        && !req.user.roles.includes('admin'))) {
        return res.status(403).json({ status: false, message: "Unauthorized" });
    }
    ...
});
```

## Severity
CRITICAL — Unauthenticated sender impersonation undermines the entire trust model of the chat system.

