const admins = await Admin.find({});
for (const admin of admins) {
  if (!admin.password.startsWith('$2')) { // Not a bcrypt hash
    admin.password = await bcryptjs.hash(admin.password, 10);
    await admin.save({ validateBeforeSave: false });
  }
}
```

Admin passwords stored in plaintext — bcrypt commented out in adminAuthResource.js
## Issue

`backend/resources/auth/adminAuthResource.js:53-54`:

```javascript
// const hashedPassword = await bcryptjs.hash(password, 10);
const admin = await Admin.create({ email, name, password: password });
```

`bcryptjs` is already imported but **the hashing line is commented out**. Every admin password is stored as plaintext in the database.

## Impact

If the MongoDB database is ever exposed (misconfigured Atlas, exported dump), all admin passwords are immediately readable. Admin accounts manage students, events, rooms, and complaints.

## Fix

Uncomment the hashing and verify on login:

```javascript
const hashedPassword = await bcryptjs.hash(password, 10);
const admin = await Admin.create({ email, name, password: hashedPassword });
```

For existing admins, add a migration that hashes all plaintext passwords:
```javascript
const admins = await Admin.find({});
for (const admin of admins) {
  if (!admin.password.startsWith('$2')) { // Not a bcrypt hash
    admin.password = await bcryptjs.hash(admin.password, 10);
    await admin.save({ validateBeforeSave: false });
  }
}
```

